  tldr: 'An Iqbal Town filing rests on three moving pieces: your declared income, whatever tax was already withheld or deducted, and an accurate asset list in the wealth statement. Salaried filings run Rs. 3,500; a business or trading return is Rs. 5,000 — everything handled remotely.',
  sections: [
    { id: 'who-files-in-iqbal-town', h: 'Who in Iqbal Town Needs to File', body: `<p>The trigger for a yearly return is simple — you're registered and something taxable is coming in, whether from salary or trade. Iqbal Town's own mix runs heavy on both salaried residents and small traders scattered across its many blocks, with straightforward personal filings sitting alongside the business ones.</p>` },
    { id: 'what-you-need', h: 'What You Need to File', body: `<ul><li>Your NTN and CNIC.</li><li>Salary certificate or business/trading income summary.</li><li>Property, bank account, and other asset details for the wealth statement.</li></ul>` },
    { id: 'the-filing-process', h: 'The Filing Process, Step by Step', body: `<p>Submission runs through FBR's IRIS portal, matching your declared income against tax already withheld and pairing it with a wealth statement for the tax year. For an Iqbal Town trader, having sales, purchase, and margin figures organized ahead of time is usually what determines whether the whole thing wraps up in a day or drags on while records get pulled together.</p>` },
    { id: 'small-trader-filing', h: 'Filing for a Small Trading Business in Iqbal Town', body: `<p>A small trading or retail business in Iqbal Town, structured as a proprietorship, reports its income through the owner's own personal return — accurately capturing purchases, sales, and margin over the tax year is what matters most for getting this filing right.</p>` },
    { id: 'multiple-block-households', h: 'Filing for Households Spread Across Iqbal Town\'s Many Blocks', body: `<p>Iqbal Town's many named blocks (Rachna, Nishtar, Awan Town, and others) don't affect the filing process itself — the mechanics are identical regardless of which specific block your address falls in; only your specific address needs to be accurately reflected.</p>` },
    { id: 'common-mistakes-iqbal-town', h: 'Mistakes That Come Up for Iqbal Town Filers', body: `<p>For trading businesses, under-declaring turnover relative to actual bank activity is the most common issue. For salaried residents, incomplete reconciliation of salary withholding is the typical gap.</p>` },
    { id: 'after-filing', h: 'What Happens After You File', body: `<p>FBR's Active Taxpayer List picks up your name once processing wraps, and that listing is what actually unlocks the lower withholding rate — on a property purchase, a vehicle, or a bank transaction — whether the return behind it was a salaried filing or a trading business's.</p>` },
    { id: 'first-time-filers-iqbal-town', h: 'Filing for the First Time in Iqbal Town', body: `<p>Whether you're a salaried resident who just crossed the taxable income threshold, or a small trader formalizing your business for the first time, a first-time Iqbal Town filing establishes the baseline your future filings build on. There's no cutoff for when you can start — filing now, even years into working or trading, is straightforward to set up, and it's better to start with an accurate first return than to keep delaying.</p>` },
    { id: 'trading-business-record-keeping', h: 'Why Iqbal Town Traders Benefit From Basic Bookkeeping', body: `<p>A small trading business in Iqbal Town doesn't need elaborate accounting software, but keeping even a simple running record of purchases, sales, and cash on hand throughout the year makes filing time significantly smoother than trying to reconstruct a year's worth of transactions from memory or scattered receipts. This habit also protects the trader if FBR ever asks for supporting detail behind a declared income figure.</p>` },
    { id: 'joint-family-businesses-iqbal-town', h: 'When an Iqbal Town Family Business Involves Several Relatives', body: `<p>Many Iqbal Town trading businesses are family-run, with parents and adult children all involved in day-to-day operations even where only one person's name is on the shop registration. For filing purposes, income generally needs to be attributed to whoever it actually belongs to — if multiple family members genuinely earn separate income from the business, this should be reflected as such rather than everything funneled through a single person's return regardless of actual roles.</p>` },
    { id: 'seasonal-income-iqbal-town', h: 'Filing When Iqbal Town Business Income Varies Seasonally', body: `<p>Some Iqbal Town trading businesses see meaningfully different income across different times of year — busier around specific seasons or events, quieter otherwise. This doesn't complicate filing itself; the full tax year's income, however unevenly it arrived, gets totaled and declared together, with no special treatment needed just because the income wasn't spread evenly across the year.</p>` },
    { id: 'moving-within-iqbal-town', h: 'What Happens to Your Filing If You Move Between Iqbal Town Blocks', body: `<p>Relocating from one Iqbal Town block to another mid-year doesn't interrupt your NTN or filing history — your return simply reflects your current address as of filing time, and there's no need to re-register or start a new filing history just because your specific block changed within the same broader neighborhood.</p>` },
    { id: 'stock-and-inventory-iqbal-town', h: 'Accounting for Inventory in an Iqbal Town Trading Filing', body: `<p>A trading business in Iqbal Town holding physical stock — clothing, hardware, general merchandise — should account for opening and closing inventory when calculating net profit for the year, not just cash coming in and out. Unsold stock sitting in the shop at year end isn't yet profit, and ignoring this distinction can distort your declared income in either direction depending on whether inventory grew or shrank over the year.</p>` },
    { id: 'multiple-shops-iqbal-town', h: 'Filing for an Owner With More Than One Iqbal Town Shop', body: `<p>An Iqbal Town trader operating more than one shop — perhaps across different blocks — combines the income from all locations into one overall business filing under their single NTN, rather than treating each shop as a separate business requiring its own registration. Keeping each location's records distinct internally still helps, even though they roll up into one combined declaration.</p>` },
    { id: 'supplier-credit-iqbal-town', h: 'Filing When Your Iqbal Town Business Buys on Supplier Credit', body: `<p>Many Iqbal Town traders buy stock on credit terms from suppliers, paying later rather than at the time of purchase. This doesn't change how business income is ultimately calculated — the goods still count toward your inventory and eventual cost of sales — but outstanding supplier credit at year end is worth noting as a liability, giving a more complete and accurate financial picture alongside your declared assets.</p>` },
    { id: 'kamboh-help', h: 'How Kamboh Associates Helps Iqbal Town Filers', body: `<p>Whichever block you're in and whether you're on a fixed salary or running a stall, we take your figures over WhatsApp and turn them into a properly filed return — Rs. 3,500 for salaried, Rs. 5,000 if trading or business income is involved.</p>` }
  ],
