    { q: 'Does Gulberg 3\'s high property values mean more scrutiny on filings?', a: 'Higher-value areas can attract more attention if declarations look inconsistent, which is exactly why accurate, complete filing matters here.' },
    { q: 'How does a Gulberg 3 partnership (AOP) file differently from a proprietorship?', a: 'A partnership has its own separate filing considerations beyond a simple proprietorship, with each partner also filing individually based on their agreed profit share — worth confirming which structure applies to you.' },
    { q: 'I rent out multiple units in Gulberg 3 — do I file separately for each one?', a: 'No — combined rental income from all your units is declared together in one return, not filed separately per unit or tenant.' },
    { q: 'I just left salaried employment to become an independent consultant in Gulberg 3 — how does my filing change?', a: 'You now track and declare business income and legitimate professional expenses instead of relying on a salary certificate, which is a meaningful shift worth getting comfortable with in that first year.' },
    { q: 'My Gulberg 3 agency bills international clients in foreign currency — how is that declared?', a: 'It gets converted to Pakistani rupees at an appropriate, consistently applied rate for filing purposes rather than declared in the original currency.' },
    { q: 'My Gulberg 3 commercial unit was vacant for part of the year — what rental income do I declare?', a: 'Only what was actually collected during the months it was occupied, not an estimated full-year figure — the property still needs reflecting as an asset regardless.' },
    { q: 'Can I deduct staff salaries at my Gulberg 3 agency from my taxable business income?', a: 'Yes — staff salary and wage costs are a legitimate business expense that reduces net taxable profit, similar to rent or utilities.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates help a Gulberg 3 business owner set up proper record-keeping going forward?', a: 'Yes — we advise on simple, practical record-keeping habits that make each subsequent year\'s filing smoother than the last.' },
    { q: 'Does Kamboh Associates handle filing for a Gulberg 3 client with both a salary and a side consulting practice?', a: 'Yes — both income sources are consolidated into one accurate personal return, properly reconciled together.' },
    { q: 'How does Kamboh Associates make sure a Gulberg 3 business filing is defensible if FBR ever asks questions?', a: 'By making sure income, expenses, and assets are declared accurately and consistently from the start, backed by whatever supporting documentation is available.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates help a Gulberg 3 client transition from an old, less organized filing approach to a cleaner one?', a: 'Yes — we review prior filings, identify what needs correcting, and set up a more consistent, accurate approach going forward.' },
    { q: 'Does a Gulberg 3 agency\'s office signage or branding cost count as a deductible business expense?', a: 'Generally yes, as a legitimate marketing or setup cost, provided it\'s documented alongside your other business expenses.' },
    { q: 'Does a Gulberg 3 agency need a separate bank account from the owner\'s personal account for filing purposes?', a: 'It\'s not strictly required for a proprietorship, though keeping a separate account makes tracking business income and expenses considerably easier at filing time.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates help a Gulberg 3 client plan ahead for next year\'s filing rather than just handling this year\'s?', a: 'Yes — we can advise on record-keeping and structural decisions now that make next year\'s filing simpler and more accurate.' },
    { q: 'Can a Gulberg 3 agency\'s international client contracts be shared in their original English form, or do they need translating?', a: 'Original English contracts are fine as supporting documentation — no translation is needed for filing purposes.' },
    { q: 'Does Kamboh Associates serve Gulberg 3 clients who work in shared co-working spaces rather than a dedicated office?', a: 'Yes — a co-working space arrangement doesn\'t change the filing process, and the address can still be reflected appropriately if it\'s used as a business address.' }
