    { q: 'How long does it take to file an Askari 11 return?', a: 'A complete, well-documented filing is typically finished within a few working days.' },
    { q: 'Do multiple earners in an Askari 11 household each need to file separately?', a: 'Yes — each individual with their own NTN files their own separate return, even within the same household.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates help coordinate my registration and first pension-income filing together?', a: 'Yes — we regularly handle both together for recently retired Askari 11 clients going through this transition for the first time.' },
    { q: 'How soon does filer status apply after filing an Askari 11 return?', a: 'It typically reflects on the Active Taxpayer List a short while after your return is processed.' },
    { q: 'Do I need to declare rental income if I rent out my Askari 11 property while posted elsewhere?', a: 'Yes — rental income needs to be declared alongside your other income when filing.' },
    { q: 'Can my spouse handle the practical side of my filing while I\'m deployed?', a: 'Yes — a spouse can manage documentation and coordination, but the filing itself is done under the serving member\'s own NTN using their own income and asset details.' },
    { q: 'How is a retirement gratuity or lump sum payment declared?', a: 'It generally has its own specific tax treatment, separate from both regular salary and ongoing pension, and should be declared correctly in the year it\'s received rather than mixed in with other income.' },
    { q: 'I receive a family pension after losing a family member who served — how do I file?', a: 'Family pension has its own filing considerations distinct from a personal pension — you\'ll need your own NTN if you don\'t already have one, and the family pension is declared as your income going forward.' },
    { q: 'My adult child grew up in Askari 11 and just started a civilian job — does their filing connect to our family\'s service record?', a: 'No — it\'s an entirely independent first-time salaried filing using only their own NTN and salary details, with no connection to a parent\'s service or filing history.' },
    { q: 'We\'re planning to sell our Askari 11 property years after retirement — when should we make sure our filing is current?', a: 'Well ahead of the sale — a clean, consistent filing history and current filer status avoid the higher non-filer withholding rate and questions about the property\'s value history.' },
    { q: 'I received a payout from an armed forces benevolent fund — how do I declare this?', a: 'It\'s worth confirming the specific tax treatment for that payout rather than assuming it follows the same rules as ordinary salary or pension income.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates coordinate filing for an entire Askari 11 family, including a serving member posted elsewhere?', a: 'Yes — we regularly coordinate multiple family members\' filings together, working remotely with a serving member wherever they\'re currently posted.' },
    { q: 'How does Kamboh Associates ensure sensitive Askari 11 family financial information stays confidential?', a: 'All communication and documentation is handled discreetly over WhatsApp, with the same confidentiality standard applied to every client regardless of background.' },
    { q: 'Does Kamboh Associates understand the specific documentation formats used by armed forces pension and benevolent fund records?', a: 'Yes — we regularly work with these specific document types and can advise on how they should be reflected in a filing.' },
    { q: 'Does a change in an Askari 11 serving member\'s rank affect how their salary is declared for filing?', a: 'No — a rank change simply means updated salary figures on the next salary certificate; the filing process itself doesn\'t change based on rank.' },
    { q: 'If an Askari 11 member is promoted or reassigned partway through the tax year, does that change how the return should be filed?', a: 'The salary or pension figures simply reflect the actual amounts received across the year — a promotion or reassignment mid-year doesn\'t require a different filing approach, just accurate total figures.' },
    { q: 'Are pension slips issued by the military accounting system accepted as-is for an Askari 11 filing?', a: 'Yes — the standard pension documentation issued through the military accounting system is accepted as supporting evidence without needing reformatting.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates advise on the timing between a serving Askari 11 member\'s posting changes and their filing deadline?', a: 'Yes — we work around a serving member\'s schedule and postings to make sure filing deadlines are still met on time.' }
